<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>The problem</h2>
    <p>Decisions get made in meetings, Slack threads and pull requests. Then they get lost.</p>
    <p>Six months later, someone asks why the system works this way. Nobody knows. The person who decided has moved on, and the reasons went with them.</p>
    <p>Some teams keep decision records. Most keep them as markdown files spread across a dozen repos, or as wiki pages nobody can find. Free tools help you write a record. Few help your team review it, approve it, and find it again.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What Cascadras will do</h2>
    <div class="features">
      <p><strong>Decision records.</strong> Write, review, approve and search. Every repo, one place. Start from Lee Atchison's templates, or bring your own.</p>
      <p><strong>Risk matrices, linked to the decisions.</strong> A risk spreadsheet gets filed away and goes stale. In Cascadras, each risk links to the decisions that create it or reduce it, and to the service it lives in.</p>
      <p><strong>Service tiers.</strong> Tag each service Tier 1 to Tier 4, or name your own tiers. The tier shows on every decision, every risk, and the map.</p>
      <p><strong>A map of who owns what.</strong> Which team owns which service, who's on call, and where the runbook is. It comes free with the records.</p>
      <p><strong>Your records stay yours.</strong> Git is the backend. Clone, pull and push. Export everything, any time. Already keep records in Nygard or MADR format? Cascadras will import them on day one.</p>
      <p><strong>Your AI tools can read them.</strong> A built-in MCP server lets Claude Code, Cursor and the rest read your decisions while they work.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <p>Engineering teams of about 10 to 50 engineers. Big enough to lose track of why things were built the way they were. Too small for a heavyweight developer portal.</p>
  </div>
</section>

